{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"3d5401f1d6b5f01a","name":"card_event_resourcefulness","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/Legions/events/card_event_resourcefulness","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"RESOURCEFULNESS","text":"Draw a random Commando unit from your deck.","flavorText":"Many Allied prisoners of war believed that it was their duty to try to escape and to rejoin the fight again. However, fewer than 1,200 of the 170,000 British and Commonwealth POWs in Germany managed to escape successfully and to make it home. One of the most famous breakouts is the “Great Escape” in 1944, lead by Squadron Leader Roger Bushell, from Stalag Luft III camp which held Allied aircrew. Preparations for the escape started in 1943, with three tunnels being dug by the POWs, but they only managed to finish one. On the night of the breakout 76 men climbed out of the tunnel, but of those only 3 made it home. The rest of the men were captured by the Germans and 50 of them were executed on Hitlers orders. This breakout was immortalized in the 1963 film “The Great Escape” although characters and events were altered.","faction":"Britain","type":"order","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":1,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_resourcefulness","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_resourcefulness_title","SourceString":"RESOURCEFULNESS","LocalizedString":"RESOURCEFULNESS"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_resourcefulness_text","SourceString":"Draw a random Commando unit from your deck.","LocalizedString":"Draw a random Commando unit from your deck."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_resourcefulness_history","SourceString":"Many Allied prisoners of war believed that it was their duty to try to escape and to rejoin the fight again. However, fewer than 1,200 of the 170,000 British and Commonwealth POWs in Germany managed to escape successfully and to make it home. One of the most famous breakouts is the “Great Escape” in 1944, lead by Squadron Leader Roger Bushell, from Stalag Luft III camp which held Allied aircrew. Preparations for the escape started in 1943, with three tunnels being dug by the POWs, but they only managed to finish one. On the night of the breakout 76 men climbed out of the tunnel, but of those only 3 made it home. The rest of the men were captured by the Germans and 50 of them were executed on Hitlers orders. This breakout was immortalized in the 1963 film “The Great Escape” although characters and events were altered.","LocalizedString":"Many Allied prisoners of war believed that it was their duty to try to escape and to rejoin the fight again. However, fewer than 1,200 of the 170,000 British and Commonwealth POWs in Germany managed to escape successfully and to make it home. One of the most famous breakouts is the “Great Escape” in 1944, lead by Squadron Leader Roger Bushell, from Stalag Luft III camp which held Allied aircrew. Preparations for the escape started in 1943, with three tunnels being dug by the POWs, but they only managed to finish one. On the night of the breakout 76 men climbed out of the tunnel, but of those only 3 made it home. The rest of the men were captured by the Germans and 50 of them were executed on Hitlers orders. This breakout was immortalized in the 1963 film “The Great Escape” although characters and events were altered."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Legions","isReserved":true,"cipher":1,"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Britain/Invasion/t_resourcefulness.t_resourcefulness","SubPathString":""},"artist":"British WWII Poster","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Ass